INT. SPEEDWAY GO-KART TRACK - PIT LANE - AFTERNOON

Tires stacked like donuts. The smell of two-stroke. A hand-lettered sign: "NO RUNNING. NO CRYING. NO REFUNDS."

MILO GALLAGHER-SINGH, 15, cracked helmet, oil on his cheek, kneels by a small yellow kart. DOMINIC TREJO, 15, in a stained racing suit two sizes big, leans on the fence and chews a straw. PRIYANKA "PINKY" DESAI, 14, clipboard, stopwatch around her neck, stands between them.

PINKY
Four minutes to the heat.

MILO
It's the carburetor.

DOMINIC
It's the driver.

MILO
It is not the driver.

PINKY
Dom, he's got a point.

DOMINIC
He always has a point, Pinky. That's his whole problem.

MILO
I can fix it.

DOMINIC
You said that at Nationals.

MILO
That was the tire!

PINKY
It was the tire.

DOMINIC
Whose tire?

MILO
Yours!

PINKY
Three minutes.

Milo slams the wrench down. Dominic pushes off the fence. They square up, nose to nose, helmet to helmet.

DOMINIC
Say it again.

MILO
Say what?

DOMINIC
That it's me.

MILO
It's the carburetor.

PINKY
Boys. Boys.

DOMINIC
Pinky, stay out of it.

PINKY
I'm the pit boss.

MILO
She's the pit boss.

DOMINIC
She's fourteen!

PINKY
I'm fourteen and a half, and I'm timing you.

A horn blares from the track. Everyone flinches. Milo grabs the wrench. Dominic grabs the steering wheel. They both pull the kart in opposite directions.

PINKY (CONT'D)
That's it. I'm calling my brother.

She raises the stopwatch. Presses it. The chaos holds. The engine coughs, sputters, and catches.

MILO
Oh.

DOMINIC
Oh.

They stare at the roaring kart. Dominic slides in. Milo hands him a glove.

DOMINIC (CONT'D)
(not looking up)
Thanks.

MILO
Don't mention it.

PINKY
Go!
